Use a new tag (v2). The chart's pullPolicy is Always, but a new tag avoids any cached v1. Then roll it out without re-applying the whole hub:
kubectl -n monitoring set image deploy/telemetry-ui \
  $(kubectl -n monitoring get deploy telemetry-ui -o jsonpath='{.spec.template.spec.containers[0].name}')=$ACR.azurecr.io/telemetry-ui:v2
kubectl -n monitoring rollout status deploy/telemetry-ui
kubectl -n monitoring logs deploy/telemetry-ui | tail
Set telemetryUi.image.tag: v2 in hub-azure.yaml too, so a later render doesn't go back to v1. Don't re-apply the hub render to roll this out, because it regenerates the ClickHouse Secrets. If you ever do render again, drop the kind: Secret documents first."

